Rombie's change to Stella (Bro Code Technologies, 2026-10-29), under Stella's GPL-2.0-or-later, for Stella 7.0c
(c4016ea): the core is built without the code Stella says it took from z26, whose license (the GPL "Version 2",
with no "or any later version") cannot be combined with RetroArch's GPL-3.0. Removed:
- the CompuMate (cartridge scheme CM and its keyboard): a CompuMate cartridge no longer loads;
- the Kid Vid, the MindLink, the Amiga mouse, the Atari mouse and the trackball: a game set to one of them gets a
  joystick;
- the mouse driving a joystick, and the trackball sensitivity setting;
- the z26 palette: choosing it gives Stella's standard palette, and the libretro option no longer offers it;
- the default Supercharger header: a 6K image now gets one written from the load format's fields.
stella/build.sh also deletes the removed classes' files (CartCM, CompuMate, KidVid, MindLink, PointingDevice,
AmigaMouse, AtariMouse, TrakBall) from the build's copy, so nothing compiled can include them.

